# Fabric Mod Guidance

- Target versions:
  - Minecraft `26.1.1`
  - Fabric Loader `0.19.2`
  - Fabric API `0.145.4+26.1.1`
- Use official Mojang mappings only. Do not answer with Yarn names unless the user explicitly asks for a cross-reference.
- Prefer Fabric documentation first for APIs, setup, data generation, mixins, networking, rendering, and other modding workflows: [Developer Guides](https://docs.fabricmc.net/develop/).
- When implementation details are unclear, inspect extracted vanilla sources from `minecraft-src` before guessing behavior.
- Treat `minecraft-src` as reference code only unless the user explicitly asks to modify it.
- Match Fabric and Mojang naming exactly when suggesting classes, methods, fields, events, registries, tags, NBT/data components, and JSON resource structures.
- Prefer Fabric-supported hooks, APIs, events, and data-driven content over invasive mixins when both approaches are viable.
- Keep examples aligned with this project's Java/Fabric setup and Gradle-based workflow.
- If documentation and decompiled source disagree, call out the mismatch and explain which source is more trustworthy for the current task.

## Good defaults

- Check Fabric docs for the feature area before inventing an approach.
- Verify vanilla behavior in `minecraft-src` when targeting entity AI, item use, NBT persistence, rendering, or registry behavior.
- Write guidance and code samples using Mojang-mapped symbols.
